msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:92
msgid "Read SEO fields"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:93
msgid "The SEO fields of one post or term as stored — an empty one falls back to the templates of its type — and what its page shows now: the title and the meta description with the templates filled in, the canonical address and whether search engines are asked not to index it. Lists only the fields the user may edit. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:106
msgid "Change SEO fields"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: the fields with their types, 2: the variables of templates.
#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:108
#, php-format
msgid "Overwrites SEO fields of one post or term: all the values given, or none if one cannot be stored (the error says what that field takes). An empty value (\"\", false, 0 for an image) clears a field, so the page falls back to the templates; fields not given stay as they are. A text may use the variables of the templates, %2$s. Returns the fields and what the page shows afterwards. The fields: %1$s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:116
msgid "Field key => new value, e.g. {\"title\": \"Prices {sep} {site}\", \"description\": \"\"}."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:126
msgid "Find posts by their SEO"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:127
msgid "Lists the posts of a post type, or the terms of a taxonomy, with their own SEO title and meta description and what their pages show: to find the pages without a meta description of their own (missing \"description\"), for example, and then change them with simple-seo/update-fields. Posts newest first, terms by name; with wp-loc, those of the default language. Paged. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:134
msgid "post or term. Default post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:138
msgid "The post type (default post) or the taxonomy (default category)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:144
msgid "Only those without an SEO title of their own (title), a meta description of their own (description), or either. Default: all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:148
msgid "Words the title or the text has (posts), or the name (terms)."
msgstr ""

