#, php-format
msgid "How many on a page: %1$d by default, %2$d at most."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:171
msgid "Analyse a post"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:172
msgid "Analyses a post as saved: the SEO checks of its focus keyphrase (the field keyphrase) and its page, and the readability of its text, each check with its status (good, ok, bad or info) and what to do, and both scores out of 100. Also the title and the description its page shows. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:178
msgid "ID of the post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:188
msgid "Google Search Console data"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: the default number of days.
#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:190
#, php-format
msgid "Google Search Console data. Without an ID, of the whole site for the last 7, 28 or 90 days that have data: clicks, impressions, CTR and average position, beside those of the period before, and the top queries and pages. With the ID of a published post, its own for %d days with its top queries. Search Console must be connected on its tab of the settings. Read-only; the answers of Google are kept for six hours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:196
msgid "ID of a published post; without it, the whole site."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: the default number of days.
#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:203
#, php-format
msgid "The period of the site: 7, 28 or 90 days (default %d)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:212
msgid "Read the settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:213
msgid "The settings of Simple SEO, row by row, with the defaults filled in: the templates of titles and descriptions, indexing, social networks, the special pages, the sitemaps, breadcrumbs, Schema, local SEO, images, integrations, IndexNow, the access of roles and the rest. With wp-loc, the rows of texts are those of the current language. The key of the Search Console service account is not given, only its account. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:220
msgid "IndexNow status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:221
msgid "Whether IndexNow sends the changes of pages to search engines, and why not if it does not; its key and key file; the addresses waiting and when they go; the last answers of Bing. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:228
msgid "Send addresses through IndexNow"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-seo-abilities.php:229
msgid "Sends addresses to search engines through IndexNow at once (to Bing; the search engines that take part share them): of posts by their IDs — only pages search engines may show, as the sitemap lists them — and addresses of this site. The addresses waiting go with them. A page published, changed or taken down is sent by itself a minute later: use this for pages changed in another way. Returns the answers of Bing and what was left out, with why."
msgstr ""

