#: includes/class-simple-seo-github-updater.php:103
msgid "Version 0.41.0: the SEO block writes the SEO title, the meta description and the focus keyphrase with AI, through the provider connected in Settings → Connectors; the variables of the template stay. Version 0.40.0: the SEO block suggests internal links: the other pages of this site that the text mentions by their keyphrase or title, without a link to them yet. Version 0.39.0: the audit lists the pages no other page links to. Version 0.38.0: the audit checks the links on the pages too, on this site and elsewhere: the broken ones, the links of this site that redirect, and a check a day later of those that did not answer. Version 0.37.0: an audit of the pages of the sitemap as a visitor sees them: titles and descriptions missing or the same, H1 headings, images without alt text, canonical addresses, noindex and pages that do not open, in the background on a page of the SEO menu. Version 0.36.0: a monitor of pages not found: the addresses that answer 404, how many times and where the visitors came from, without IP addresses, on a page of the SEO menu, and a draft redirect of the WP Base theme from one in a click. Version 0.35.0: tools for AI agents through Simple MCP: the SEO fields of posts and terms, the pages without a title or description of their own, the analysis, Search Console, the settings and IndexNow. Version 0.34.0: WP-CLI commands (wp simple-seo) for the SEO fields of posts and terms, the analysis, the imports and IndexNow, and the SEO fields of every post type and taxonomy in the REST API. Version 0.33.0: IndexNow: a page published, changed, moved or taken down is sent to Bing a minute later, so search engines visit it sooner; and Yandex is no longer supported. Version 0.32.0: Google Search Console in the admin: the clicks, impressions, CTR and position of the site with its top queries and pages on a page of the SEO menu, and those of each post in its SEO box, read with the key of a service account of Google. Version 0.31.0: the Integrations tab: codes of webmaster tools on the home page, taken from Yoast SEO, Rank Math and All in One SEO, and the tags of Google Analytics, Google Tag Manager, Meta Pixel and TikTok Pixel, loaded on the visitor's first move and waiting for consent when asked. Version 0.30.0: the description made from the text of a post and the length checks of the content analysis go by the width search results give, not by a number of characters. Version 0.29.0: alt texts and titles of images from their names, on upload and in bulk editing for the images already uploaded. Version 0.28.0: Local SEO: the type of the organization, its address, phone, opening hours and place on the map in the Schema graph, taken from Rank Math, Yoast SEO, All in One SEO or the theme. Version 0.27.0: JSON-LD of its own for a post or a term, added to its graph. Version 0.26.0: the type of page and of article of each post and post type, and FAQ pages from the questions and answers of theme blocks, accordions or the new block Questions and answers. Version 0.25.0: Schema structured data, one JSON-LD graph of the site, whom it represents, the page, the article and the breadcrumb trail, in the mode Auto silent where the theme prints its own. Version 0.24.0: bulk editing of SEO titles and descriptions in a table, for whoever edits the SEO fields. Version 0.23.0: readability of the text with a score of its own, and a column with the SEO and readability scores in the lists of posts. Version 0.22.0: the import takes the keyphrases of Yoast SEO, Rank Math and All in One SEO too. Version 0.21.0: content analysis in the SEO block of posts: a focus keyphrase and more, checks of the page for them and a score. Version 0.20.0: groundwork for the content analysis: Simple SEO reads the text of a page from any editor, ACF and Builder blocks included. Version 0.19.0: a search result preview above the SEO fields of posts and terms, on a computer and on a phone, redone as you type. Version 0.18.0: the Import tab takes over the settings and the SEO fields of All in One SEO too, and removes what AIOSEO left in the database. Version 0.17.0: the Import tab takes over the settings and the SEO fields of Rank Math too, and removes what Rank Math left in the database. Version 0.16.0: the Import tab also removes what Yoast SEO left in the database once its data is imported, part by part, after a backup is confirmed. Version 0.15.0: the Import tab takes over the settings of Yoast SEO and the SEO fields of posts and terms, leaving Simple SEO's own values as they are. Version 0.14.0: the Yoast SEO post meta themes read and write (_yoast_wpseo_title, _yoast_wpseo_metadesc and the like) is Simple SEO's own fields. Version 0.13.0: the Yoast SEO filters themes hook into (title, description, Open Graph, robots, breadcrumbs, sitemaps) change Simple SEO's output. Version 0.12.0: themes made for Yoast SEO keep working without it: wpseo_replace_vars(), yoast_breadcrumb() and WPSEO_Primary_Term are answered by Simple SEO. Version 0.11.0: llms.txt for AI assistants, built from the pages search engines may show, one for each language under wp-loc. Version 0.10.0: the Clean-up tab removes the WordPress version, shortlink, discovery links, emoji script and feed links from pages, each by its own switch. Version 0.9.0: robots.txt and .htaccess edited on the Files tab, with a history of versions; a .htaccess that takes the site down is put back at once. Version 0.8.0: breadcrumbs for themes (PHP, Twig, shortcode) with their own tab, and the primary category of a post. Version 0.7.0: XML sitemap at the addresses Yoast SEO used, a sitemap for each language under wp-loc. Version 0.6.0: settings for the home page, the 404 page and password-protected content. Version 0.5.0: Open Graph and X card. Version 0.4.0: canonical address, noindex and nofollow. Version 0.3.0: page title and meta description from fields and templates. While another SEO plugin is active, nothing is printed."
msgstr ""

